00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:05.100
Episode Fifteen: 
I Don't Understand 

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:03.060
And today the new semester starts.

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:06.650
From here on, humanity will face a time when they fly into the universe.

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:08.880
On your shoulders...

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:13.460
...lies the anticipation of being the frontrunners for humanity.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:15.860
But instead of feeling pressure from that...

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:17.730
...I want you to walk on with pride.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:21.790
The opening ceremony is two months late, but I feel that for each of you...

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:24.400
...even during the period you were waiting back home...

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.660
...you didn't lose your discipline, and you endeavored to "level up".

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:28.140
It would be embarrassing...

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:30.740
...if the only thing that went up was the size of your waists.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.540
Hey, Masaru, he's talking about you.

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:36.060
Well, I am at that growing stage right now.

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:39.070
It's certainly acceptable for my weight to fluctuate.

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:43.030
If anything, the problem is the accumulation of stress...

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:44.880
...that comes along with restraining yourself.

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:45.770
Hey now.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:48.230
Your quibbling is "leveling up".

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:52.930
Dai-chan really is funny.

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:58.030
Kouta?

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:03.010
Oh, sorry.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:05.700
Oh, you're hopeless.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:09.630
But we should listen to the headmaster's speech right now.

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:11.880
Oh, that's right. I'm sorry.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:28.730
A mock battle?

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:32.710
Are you saying we should make the students play at being at war?

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.080
Of course, they can operate the Ora-avis machines.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.700
The Great Mission taught them marksmanship.

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:38.920
And the Joust taught them dog fighting.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.150
In other words, they've already learned...

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:42.840
...the necessary basic skills to fight a war.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:45.660
All they have to do is train under real combat conditions...

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.520
...and they'll be able to react to any surprise circumstances.

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:51.070
And what would "surprise circumstances" be?

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:56.620
Two months have already passed...

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:59.590
...since the detection of the first unidentified flying object.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:03.210
In that time, the flying objects have been detected...

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:06.310
...not just at the Ultima, but also at the Akapusu and the El Santo.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:10.500
Maintaining the safety of the Stellvia is the duty of us adults, right?

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.840
We must maintain the safety, Not just of the Stellvia...

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.680
...but of the entire universe.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:17.710
The entire universe?

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:18.740
That's right.

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:22.040
The Stellvia, as the leader of the universe...

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:25.050
...has the responsibility to supervise the other Foundations.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:40.730
What the... Shipon, you're wearing an unfamiliar chest protector.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:42.740
Did you buy it?

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:46.940
I bought it two days ago, by myself.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:51.270
For Kouta?

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:56.850
W-W-W-W-What are you saying, Miss Glennorth?

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:59.200
That couldn't possibly be.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:02.060
Just dressing up, dressing up. A bit of a challenge...

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:05.760
What are you getting all formal for, girl?

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:08.360
W-Well, we are sixteen years old...

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.440
But that will have to wait until we're adults.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:13.650
And Kouta couldn't possibly want that...

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:15.790
No one said anything about that

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:20.710
Well, that's fine. But you know, all boys are lechers.

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:22.240
Kouta is different!

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:23.890
If both people love each other...

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:26.120
...it's not strange to do that at sixteen, right?

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:26.520
What?

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:28.840
Oh, just what I'd expect from Milady!

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:30.550
An adult point of view!

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:34.210
Even students can legally get married, after all!

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:35.860
Um...

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:37.730
Speaking of which, what about you, Milady?

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:40.500
How have things gone with Pierre since then?

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:42.720
Do you think they've gone anywhere?

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:43.990
I don't.

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:45.780
Absolutely correct.

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:47.950
Aw...

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:50.490
Don't you have someone you like or anything, Arisa?

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:51.300
Hmm?

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.480
Well, for now, that's impossible.

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:58.940
Shipon's already taken Kouta, and Dai-chan is out of the question.

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:03.860
Pierre just has his looks, and along those lines, Jojo is an idiot, so...

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:05.090
That's not true.

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:05.880
What?

00:06:06.460 --> 00:06:07.410
That's not...

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:10.450
He reads books and stuff a lot.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.930
And, yeah, his grades are bad, but...

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.400
Akira!
Whoa!

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:22.220
W-Wait a second.

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:23.920
How far have you gone?

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:29.440
W-What?

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:33.380
We have something we would like to ask you, Mr. Kouta Otoyama.

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:34.850
We do!

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:36.910
Please be sure to answer, no matter what.

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:41.010
How far have you gone with Shipon?

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:41.620
What?

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:43.290
And please don't use the expected silliness...

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:45.580
...like, "to an amusement park" or anything.

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:48.240
Y-You've kissed her at least, right?

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:48.960
Yeah.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:50.260
Whoa!
Whoa!

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:53.880
W-Well, going at least that far would be natural.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:56.110
We're not in elementary school, after all.

00:06:56.920 --> 00:06:57.730
What about you, Pierre?

00:06:57.900 --> 00:06:58.780
What, me?!

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:02.550
W-When I was fourteen, I guess.

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:04.060
Fourteen!

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:05.760
I was fourteen, too!

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:07.760
How unexpected.

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:10.850
Wow, you guys did it early.

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:13.630
W-Well, that's normal.

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:15.080
Y-Yeah, that's true.

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:19.330
But more important than early or late, is who you do it with.

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:21.350
Yeah, that's true.

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:24.530
Oh, I still haven't... kissed yet...

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.010
Masaru!
Masaru!

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:36.560
This is your first training session in two months.

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:38.560
Don't worry about your time.

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:41.160
Just try to get back your intuition.

00:07:41.590 --> 00:07:42.690
Next, Katase!

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:43.360
Yes, ma'am!

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:56.170
She's ping-ponging along as always.

00:07:56.690 --> 00:07:58.740
The break didn't affect her.

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:01.970
A long time ago, I used to be better, though.

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:04.060
That's from ancient times.

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:06.010
At least call it the Middle Ages.

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:07.410
Look.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:09.530
Those are armed Katies.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:10.650
You're right.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:13.170
Things are starting to get really spirited.

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:15.660
They really do seem like fighters.

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:16.990
They're so cool.

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:18.810
Spirited things are so cool.

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:22.710
I think it's easier to control them without anything attached, though.

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:26.210
Doesn't matter... It's not like we're going to be piloting them.

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:28.410
Next, Joy Jones! 
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:31.010
Please let us help, too!

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:35.380
We can at least handle patrolling.

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:36.650
Right, Syoujin?

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:39.070
But...

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:41.330
We have confidence in controlling the Katies.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:44.830
And during the Second Wave, we finished our marksmanship training.

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:46.130
Right, Syoujin?

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:49.950
You mustn't forget your own true duties.

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:51.920
Your studies should be your priority.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:55.240
Leave what's going on outside the school to us.

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:56.510
But...

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:58.160
Hey, Syoujin...

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:02.040
We are members of the Stellvia, too.

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:02.760
Hmm...?

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:06.980
We want to protect our school ourselves.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:10.740
What? You're not going, Akira?

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:13.350
I'm on cleaning duty today.

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:16.380
I see. It's our first day, and you're unlucky already.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:19.650
Hey... Masaru.

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:22.390
You said you're on cleaning duty today, right?

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:24.020
I'll swap with you.

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:28.120
That's all right. It's not like I have any special plans after this.

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:31.070
Don't say something like that. Swap with me, please!

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:32.600
Argh, Again?
Masaru!

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:48.880
H-Hey, Kouta...

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:51.540
Kouta. Kouta!

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:52.060
What?

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:54.120
Oh...

00:09:57.640 --> 00:10:00.420
After we finish getting changed, want to go see a movie together?

00:10:00.970 --> 00:10:01.460
A movie?

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:04.410
They're playing Evun Saumur's new picture.

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:07.530
You said you liked his work before, right, Kouta?

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:08.720
Oh...

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:13.580
I'm sorry. They asked me to monitor the new system after this.

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:15.370
What, again?

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:16.820
It can't be helped.

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:20.690
Right now, the only one who can do it is me.

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:22.630
You can't get a break?

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:25.450
It's been decided since last week, so...

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:30.670
I understand!

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:37.570
Sa       do

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:31.060
Mono

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:32.810
In baseball, the term is 'game set'.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:34.630
So what is it in rugby? Five characters.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:37.250
No Side "No side."

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:40.560
What kind of bird is always in the limelight in the newspaper?

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:41.920
Two characters.

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:43.940
Kiji.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:45.960
A job for men.

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:48.710
It's recently been the topic of discussion throughout the universe.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:49.690
Two characters...

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:51.570
Hmm...

00:10:52.180 --> 00:10:54.410
It's not a space pilot or anything.

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:56.170
Recently...

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:57.500
Recently.

00:10:57.650 --> 00:10:58.600
Oh, I've got it.

00:10:59.090 --> 00:10:59.730
It's a himo.

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:00.860
Himo?

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:03.370
You know, the giant himo that has become visible...

00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:04.780
...in the direction of the constellation Hydra.

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:06.290
It's become news recently, right?

00:11:06.610 --> 00:11:07.450
Right.

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:09.680
They call it a himo, but it's really a warping of space, right?

00:11:09.970 --> 00:11:11.900
They say it's an aftereffect of the Second Wave.

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:13.900
It might have been there beforehand...

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:17.110
...and we couldn't see it because the Second Wave was obscuring it.

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:21.360
A gigantic, 3-billion-kilometer space himo in the red universe.

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:23.980
The astronomical show has gotten crowded.

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:26.650
"Himo" = "string" or "pimp" 

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:26.650
But is being a himo a job?

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:29.040
Oh, no, it's already late.

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:30.440
Got plans?

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:32.460
Yeah, I have a date after this.

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:33.160
Wha...

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:36.180
Didn't you say you broke up with the guy from Christmas?

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:38.910
Saying "broke up" is so scandalous.

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:41.170
We never even went as far as going out.

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:44.260
Someone who doesn't make you feel the difference in age is good.

00:11:44.810 --> 00:11:48.020
But maybe I'll try to act like an older sister...

00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:51.660
The person I'm going to see is a young boy, so what do you think?

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:53.670
Does it look like I'm trying to look younger?

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:56.580
Thanks.

00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:58.980
Oh, you can go ahead and solve that.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:06.030
Himo

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:30.310
Sign "Opposed to the establishment of a space military force"

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:30.240
We are opposed to the establishment of a space military force!

00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:33.560
The unidentified flying objects are fakes.

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:35.790
What? They aren't aliens?

00:12:36.050 --> 00:12:37.790
You are a dummy.

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:41.230
The question is, which Foundation is the culprit?

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:44.200
But no one has made any statements.

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:46.460
There isn't anyone who will.

00:12:46.920 --> 00:12:50.710
Enforcing any policy will only stir up opposition between the Foundations.

00:12:51.090 --> 00:12:52.530
A war in space?

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:55.050
Well, war itself doesn't do anything for me.

00:12:55.190 --> 00:12:57.330
Oh, I saw that in a movie recently.

00:12:57.770 --> 00:13:01.150
It went bazap, bah-bah-bah-bah-bah, shimmer-shimmer-shimmer!

00:12:57.880 --> 00:12:59.170
A space... war?

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:02.680
Isn't it impossible to have a war without an army?

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:03.930
You were watching a pretty old movie.

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:03.810
Really?

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:06.180
"Shimmer-shimmer" is what a caterpillar does, right?

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:06.380
If you fight with weapons, isn't that a war?

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:09.590
That's not it. A "katabira" is what they wear in period films, right?

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:08.320
I don't think that's it.

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:10.870
I see...

00:13:10.230 --> 00:13:10.840
I said "caterpillar"!

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:15.000
In our lecture, they said that it was a war when two nations fought.

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:13.120
Oh, I've seen another one! 

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:14.080
What is it this time... 

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:17.110
It went bazap, bah-bah-bah-bah-bah, shimmer-shimmer-shimmer!

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:18.560
And there stopped being nations 120 years ago, too.

00:13:17.140 --> 00:13:17.690
It's the same...

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:20.000
This is reality we're talking about. 

00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:21.680
Then a war is when a lot of people fight with a lot of other people!

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:21.710
It would be embarrassing for you to mix it up with a movie. 

00:13:22.370 --> 00:13:24.230
And how many people is a lot?

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:25.560
And this idiot is why I didn't want to be on this show.

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:25.670
Um...

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:27.460
Oh, you're mean!

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:28.190
Being conservative... about 1,000 people?

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:29.100
And here we'll take a short break.

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:34.580
A new picture starring Evun Saumur:

00:13:35.010 --> 00:13:35.970
"First Wave"

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:38.310
"The Love That Carried Throughout the Universe"

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:43.220
Currently playing to rave reviews.

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:46.430
Shipon, are you a fan of Evun's?

00:13:46.780 --> 00:13:47.970
N-No.

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:51.000
You were planning on seeing that with Kouta, right?

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:51.490
What?

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:54.410
Oh! So we're just stand-ins.

00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:55.980
I-It's nothing like that.

00:13:56.180 --> 00:14:00.110
That's all right. Friendship between girls is a fickle thing.

00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:01.560
Arisa!

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:04.770
Hey, wouldn't it be a good idea to set up rules, like in sports?

00:14:04.970 --> 00:14:06.530
Oh, that might be good!

00:14:06.590 --> 00:14:07.460
It's time for a commercial.

00:14:08.810 --> 00:14:11.710
It appears they don't really understand what war is.

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:13.500
It can't be helped.

00:14:14.250 --> 00:14:17.460
Right now, after all, there isn't even one person on the Earth...

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:19.200
...who has experienced war.

00:14:20.350 --> 00:14:21.680
But we have weapons.

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:24.750
Even angels carry bows.

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:28.680
Whether or not it becomes a weapon depends on the user.

00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:32.300
Up until now, we had a common enemy called the Second Wave.

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:34.840
But now that it's gone...

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:39.700
Last time we came here, I got some discount coupons.

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:41.900
You came with Kouta, right?

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:44.960
You don't deny anything, do you?

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:48.370
Welcome!

00:14:48.630 --> 00:14:50.600
Oh, cut it out. 
Really, you...

00:14:52.710 --> 00:14:54.010
What's wrong, Yayoi?

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:57.110
H-Hey, Shipon, how about we go to a different shop?

00:14:57.190 --> 00:14:57.480
What?

00:14:58.030 --> 00:15:00.140
I found this really cute place the other day.

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:03.580
But the coupons are only good until tomorrow...

00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:10.410
Oh, man...

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:12.430
Shipon, wait a second!

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:15.840
I wonder if people see us as lovers.

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:18.910
I think, at best, they see us as brother and sister.

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:20.610
You're so coldhearted.

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:21.420
Hmm?

00:15:22.260 --> 00:15:22.700
Oh.

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:24.460
Miss Katase.

00:15:27.180 --> 00:15:27.640
Heya.

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:30.360
What's wrong?

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:32.850
W-W-Well...

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:34.410
How are you?

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:36.460
Yeah, I'm doing all right.

00:15:36.690 --> 00:15:39.500
H-H-H-Has anything changed since then?

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:41.260
I'm doing fine.

00:15:41.610 --> 00:15:42.820
B-Being fine...

00:15:43.690 --> 00:15:45.080
Being fine means having the will to do something...

00:15:45.370 --> 00:15:48.230
And having the will to do something is courage... er, um...

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:49.590
Shipon, calm down.

00:15:49.990 --> 00:15:51.820
You're starting to make no sense.

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:52.650
Oh!

00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:54.110
Well...

00:15:54.740 --> 00:15:55.260
Ahem!

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:58.210
Kouta, how was the monitoring?

00:15:58.610 --> 00:16:00.380
That starts at six o'clock.

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:02.370
But I asked you to see a movie with me.

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:03.870
But it starts at six.

00:16:04.570 --> 00:16:06.320
If I went to the movie, I wouldn't make it in time.

00:16:17.090 --> 00:16:17.840
That's fine.

00:16:18.390 --> 00:16:20.010
Then I'll watch the movie by myself!

00:16:20.070 --> 00:16:21.660
What? Wait a second, Shipon!

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:24.950
She's fast!

00:16:25.070 --> 00:16:27.330
She's been working hard on her running recently.

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:29.290
She's certainly grown up.

00:16:30.560 --> 00:16:32.010
Is it all right for you not to follow her?

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:34.900
We haven't finished our talk yet, after all.

00:16:36.350 --> 00:16:40.420
You examine my body every week for the monitor test, right, ma'am?

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:42.650
Are there any abnormalities?

00:16:43.090 --> 00:16:44.790
Like brainwaves or vision?

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:46.240
There are no problems.

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:48.260
You are the very model of an extremely healthy person.

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:49.740
I see.

00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:52.770
It wasn't my imagination then...

00:16:59.770 --> 00:17:04.080
And then, Masaru, that jerk, he smeared curry inside the helmet...

00:17:07.690 --> 00:17:09.430
Oh, so they've returned.

00:17:10.010 --> 00:17:10.590
Wow.

00:17:10.850 --> 00:17:13.270
When you really look at it, it even has a laser pod attached.

00:17:13.770 --> 00:17:15.160
It's so cool.

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:17.350
It really is a man's romanticism.

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:19.290
Jojo, I...

00:17:19.870 --> 00:17:20.730
Relax.

00:17:21.280 --> 00:17:24.000
When the time comes, I'll protect you, even if it costs me my life.

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:26.460
Just kidding.

00:17:28.720 --> 00:17:30.620
To lose your life in battle...

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:33.720
Is that a cool thing?

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:42.770
The Infinity's existence is making the guys in the security force bold.

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:46.790
It was bad to have the supreme council meeting at the Stellvia.

00:17:47.310 --> 00:17:49.620
It's stirred up ideas that we have special privileges.

00:17:50.140 --> 00:17:52.490
What would come from the Foundations fighting each other?

00:17:53.120 --> 00:17:55.750
They're concerned about who's going to seize leadership, right?

00:17:56.530 --> 00:17:58.010
At the combined conference...

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:01.880
...I hear that the Akapusu and the El Santo are scuffling.

00:18:02.030 --> 00:18:03.590
It's such trifling sectarianism.

00:18:04.570 --> 00:18:08.220
But if we're not careful, the fight might not be trifling.

00:18:11.430 --> 00:18:14.000
For me to try and stop a fight...

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:15.730
If Ren heard that, she'd probably laugh.

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:18.970
What's wrong?

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:20.830
Uh... No, it's nothing.

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:23.920
Isn't it normal to say, "I can't do a movie...

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:26.330
...but how about we get some tea or something together?"

00:18:26.950 --> 00:18:30.370
Despite that, Kouta's just... What do you think, Rinna?

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:32.620
First of all, Kouta isn't conscious enough...

00:18:32.800 --> 00:18:35.690
...of us being boyfriend and girlfriend.

00:18:35.980 --> 00:18:37.570
Just recently, by himself, he...

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:38.610
Huh?

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:41.790
A phone call addressed to Shima Katase has arrived.

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:43.450
Would you like to view it?

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:44.750
Oh, yeah.

00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:48.580
Ya-Ho! It's Rinna!

00:18:49.050 --> 00:18:49.880
Rinna!

00:18:50.260 --> 00:18:52.460
I've finally arrived at the Ultima...

00:18:52.570 --> 00:18:55.000
...but apparently, I have to come back to the Stellvia again.

00:18:55.410 --> 00:18:55.840
What?

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:57.950
I mean, there's been a disturbance...

00:18:57.980 --> 00:18:59.920
...because of the unidentified flying objects, right?

00:19:00.180 --> 00:19:00.760
That's why...

00:19:01.420 --> 00:19:03.070
It's become necessary to dispatch a convoy...

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:07.210
...to take some of the residents of the Ultima onto the Stellvia.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:12.240
The staff has requested the cooperation of some students.

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:15.010
Those members are:

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:17.850
Kouta Otoyama, Shima Katase...

00:19:18.020 --> 00:19:22.680
...Ritsuo Syoujin, Kent Austin, Ayaka Machida, Najima Gebourg...

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:28.920
Shipon's late.

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:30.280
I wonder if she's all right.

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:32.970
It looked like it was quite a shock to her.

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:36.270
I thought it would be best to leave her alone, but...

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:37.570
Um...

00:19:38.350 --> 00:19:39.770
Could you hand me the sauce?

00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:43.080
T-Thanks.

00:19:44.770 --> 00:19:47.230
Doesn't the mood feel kind of serious?

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:48.330
Really?

00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:51.650
Hey, hey, everyone!

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:54.280
Rinna said she's coming back!

00:19:54.740 --> 00:19:55.610
Shipon!

00:19:56.020 --> 00:19:56.710
Welcome back.

00:19:57.950 --> 00:19:59.050
Sorry I'm late.

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:02.380
Now let's eat. I'm hungry.

00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:05.210
Excuse me! One Andro Pot-Au-Feu, please!

00:20:05.790 --> 00:20:07.470
So you said that Rinna's coming back?

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:10.450
Yeah. Because of the unidentified flying objects.

00:20:10.650 --> 00:20:13.630
But Rinna had just arrived at the Ultima, right?

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:16.660
So she's catapulting straight back? It must be tough.

00:20:16.840 --> 00:20:18.110
Yeah, that's why...

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:19.930
Let's throw a welcoming party!

00:20:25.170 --> 00:20:26.520
Yeah, let's!

00:20:26.610 --> 00:20:28.750
So she'll be arriving here around April?

00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:31.010
Then we'll have to make spring food.

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:32.890
What do we do about decorations?

00:20:33.260 --> 00:20:36.120
We want something with impact. Something that starts with a bang.

00:20:36.180 --> 00:20:36.820
Something that explodes!

00:20:37.280 --> 00:20:38.470
That's dangerous.

00:20:38.930 --> 00:20:40.120
How about a masquerade party?

00:20:40.430 --> 00:20:41.760
What about a song or something?

00:20:42.020 --> 00:20:43.430
All of us singing as a chorus.

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:46.270
So when Rinna comes in, we all sing at once.

00:20:46.450 --> 00:20:47.470
Yeah, a chorus!

00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:49.800
Jojo, you're singing, too.

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:51.100
R-Right!

00:20:51.570 --> 00:20:53.730
Let's all... sing together.

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:01.050
Yeah, let's.

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:04.520
Well then, leave the lyrics to me.

00:21:04.900 --> 00:21:05.850
All right, we have!

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:07.120
What about instruments?

00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:09.000
I can play the piano...

00:21:09.230 --> 00:21:10.880
Let's borrow the organ from the music room.

00:21:11.030 --> 00:21:12.760
And since we're going this far, let's dance!

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:15.020
Wow, somehow it seems like a musical!

00:21:16.260 --> 00:21:17.270
Then let's dance!

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:18.370
Okay, let's!

00:21:28.380 --> 00:21:29.070
Again...

00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:30.370
I can see it again.

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:31.620
What?

00:21:32.080 --> 00:21:32.740
What are you able to see?

00:21:33.930 --> 00:21:35.640
On the other side of this space himo...

00:21:36.530 --> 00:21:38.300
...I can see a faint voice.

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:40.640
A voice? Not sound?

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:41.790
It's a voice.

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:45.290
That can't be. There's no one on the other side.

00:21:45.730 --> 00:21:47.170
But I can see it.

00:21:48.990 --> 00:21:51.920
There's someone on the other side.

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
kono sora no iku hate ni

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
Where the end of this sky goes

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
この空の行く果てに

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
mada mienu mirai no nami ga ri

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
Are waves of the future that cannot yet be seen

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
まだ見えぬ 未来の波があり

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
ikite iru ikutsu mono unmei o koete yuku

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
We are alive; we overcome many destinies

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
生きている いくつもの運命を越えて行く

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
dare ni osowari dare ni koute iru no darou

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
Who are we learning from, who are we asking?

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
誰に教わり 誰に請うているのだろう

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
hito wa tsukiru inochi no aima ni

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
People do not have time to fear encountering

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
人は尽きる命の合間に

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
deau koto ni obieru ma wa nai

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
The space between expiring lives

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
出会うことに 怯える間はない

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
tatoe kyou de kono sekai ga owarou to shite ite mo

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
Even if this world would end today

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
たとえ今日で この世界が終わろうとしていても

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
kimi o ai suru darou

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
I will still love you

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
君を愛するだろう

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:07.030
Next Episode

00:23:05.740 --> 00:23:06.320
This is Shima!

00:23:06.430 --> 00:23:06.880
This is Arisa! 

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:09.670
This is Arisa! It's sudden, but Shipon is leaving the Stellvia.

00:23:09.730 --> 00:23:11.640
Everyone, thank you for taking care of me.

00:23:11.900 --> 00:23:15.370
That's not it! I'm going to the Ultima to get Rinna.

00:23:15.480 --> 00:23:17.360
What the...? The spaceship certainly is ominous...

00:23:17.450 --> 00:23:19.040
...being equipped with lots of weapons and things.

00:23:19.100 --> 00:23:20.750
Well, it is an escort mission for the most part.

00:23:20.780 --> 00:23:22.630
Oh, and she answered so casually.

00:23:22.710 --> 00:23:26.360
And thus, on the next episode of Stellvia of the Universe, "In Doubt."

00:23:26.470 --> 00:23:30.170
You said "doubt". Did I do anything, Arisa?

00:23:30.170 --> 00:23:31.220
Aren't you going to be doing it after this?

00:23:31.270 --> 00:23:33.410
What? What am I going to do?

00:23:32.050 --> 00:23:35.050
Episode Sixteen:
 In Doubt

00:23:33.460 --> 00:23:34.500
Huh... I can't say.
